  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Arvind vs Indore Municipal Corporation on 10 January, 2024 Author: Pranay Verma Bench: Pranay Verma 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Indore Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Pranay Verma On The 10 th Of January, 2024 Misc . Criminal Case No. 57545 of 2023 Between:- Arvind S/O Shri Purushottam Goyal, Aged About 52 Years, Occupation: Business R/O 17/3 Parsi Mohalla Indore (Madhya Pradesh) (By Shri Ramakant Sharma - Advocate) And Indore Municipal Corporation Through Food Inspector G.H. Bhatia Indore Municipal Corporation Indore (Madhya Pradesh) This application coming on for admission this day, the following: Order",
    "facts": "By this petition preferred under Section 482 of the Cr.P.C., the petitioner has challenged the proceedings of the trial pending before the Special Judge (Indore Municipal Corporation, Indore) vide RCT No.2627902/2009 for offences punishable under Sections 2(ia) (c) (d) (m), 2(ix)(a)(c)(e)(g)(k), 7(i)(ii) (v) and 16(i)a(i)(ii) Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954. 02. From the record, it is apparent that the complaint was filed in the year 2009 and the petitioner was arrayed as an accused therein than itself. Specific allegations were made against him at page No.3 of the complaint and the reasons were also mentioned therein as to why he has been made an accused. The proceedings before the Court remained pending for 12 years and thereafter the statement on behalf of the respondent through its Officer was recorded on 15.01.2021 in which also allegation has Arvind vs Indore Municipal Corporation on 10 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/118104885/ 1 been levelled against the petitioner. This petition for quashment of the proceedings has been filed three years after recording of such statement.",
    "arguments": "03. The contention of the learned counsel for the petitioner as to whether the petitioner is involved in the case and whether there is any material to proceed with against him are not liable to be considered in this petition under Section 482 of the Cr.P.C. particularly when the proceedings were instituted in 2009 and have already commenced.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "03. The contention of the learned counsel for the petitioner as to whether the petitioner is involved in the case and whether there is any material to proceed with against him are not liable to be considered in this petition under Section 482 of the Cr.P.C. particularly when the proceedings were instituted in 2009 and have already commenced.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
